Call Skills with "/" and Agents with "@"

Agents:
proof-generator:
Writes or revises a proof, counterexample or stuck report by following workflows/proof-workflow.md. It saves its work in proof-exchange/<problem-name>/ and does not do the independent review.

proof-reviewer:
Strictly and independently checks a written proof for errors and gaps, then gives the verdict ACCEPT or REJECT. It judges only the problem and the written proof, not the generator's reasoning.

proof-simplifier:
Checks a written proof for errors, then tries to shorten it with other techniques, simpler terminology and removal of unnecessary claims. It never changes candidate.md: it adds simplified-proof.md and simplification-report.md to the same proof-exchange/<problem-name>/ folder. It stops if the original has a critical error, works alone and is not part of prove-agent.

Skills:
prove-workflow:
Runs the full proof workflow in the main session: analyse, clarify, plan, try techniques, write, review and deliver. Usage: /prove-workflow <problem>

prove-agent:
Runs the same process with agents: proof-generator writes, proof-reviewer checks (at most 3 rounds), and they exchange files in proof-exchange/. The final result is copied to outputs/ or drafts/. Usage: /prove-agent <problem>

